#  SD-WAN with DSCP — Cheat Sheet

> **FortiGate / FortiOS — SD-WAN DSCP Steering, ECMP & Application-Based Routing**

---

## 1. SD-WAN Rule with DSCP

DSCP can be used as a matching criterion in an SD-WAN service/rule.

```bash
config system sdwan
    config service
        edit 5
            set name VoIP-Steer
            set mode priority
            set tos 0x70
            set tos-mask 0xf0
            set dst all
            set health-check Default_DNS
            set link-cost-factor jitter
            set priority-members 4 3
        end
    end
end
```

### DSCP Matching

| Parameter          |         Value | Meaning                             |
| ------------------ | ------------: | ----------------------------------- |
| `tos`              |        `0x70` | TOS/DSCP value used for matching    |
| `tos-mask`         |        `0xf0` | Mask used to identify relevant bits |
| `mode`             |    `priority` | Select members based on priority    |
| `health-check`     | `Default_DNS` | SLA/health-check object             |
| `link-cost-factor` |      `jitter` | Prefer link based on jitter         |
| `priority-members` |         `4 3` | Member 4 preferred over member 3    |

### Important

```text
DSCP/TOS
   ↓
SD-WAN Service Match
   ↓
SLA / Quality Evaluation
   ↓
Priority Members
   ↓
Selected SD-WAN Link
```

