# 7. Longest Prefix Match + SD-WAN

Example routing table:

```text
0.0.0.0/0
    → sdwan-1
    AD 1

0.0.0.0/0
    → sdwan-2
    AD 1

192.168.102.0/24
    → port-1
    AD 1
```

The specific route:

```text
192.168.102.0/24
```

has a longer prefix than:

```text
0.0.0.0/0
```

Therefore:

```text
192.168.102.0/24
        ↓
Longest Prefix Match
        ↓
port-1
```

### Key Point

> A specific route can influence which SD-WAN member/egress path is considered.

