# 10. Lowest Cost vs Best Quality

## Lowest Cost

With **Lowest Cost**, the decision is based on SLA/cost.

Important behavior:

```text
Longest-match routes
        ↓
Egress members
        ↓
SLA / Cost evaluation
        ↓
Lowest-cost valid decision
```

> Even if specific-route egress ports are outside SLA, the SD-WAN rule can still select the first/configured or lower-cost egress port from those specific-route ports.

---

## Best Quality

With **Best Quality**, quality metrics have higher importance.

```text
Latency
Packet Loss
Jitter
     ↓
Quality Calculation
     ↓
Best Quality Member
```

> Even if members on less-specific routes have better quality, a best-quality SD-WAN decision can remain constrained by the egress ports associated with the more-specific route.

---

# 11. Application Category in SD-WAN Rule

SD-WAN rules can use Internet Service / Application Control categories.

Example:

```bash
config system sdwan
    config service
        edit 1
            set mode sla
            set src 192.168.101.0/24
            set internet-service enable
            set internet-service-app-ctrl-category 5 21
        end
    end
end
```

Example categories:

```text
Category 5
    Video / Audio

Category 21
    Email
```

Concept:

```text
Client
  |
  v
Application Identification
  |
  +---- Video / Audio
  |
  +---- Email
  |
  v
SD-WAN Rule
  |
  v
SLA / Strategy
  |
  v
WAN Member
```

