# 12. Firewall Policy for Application-Based SD-WAN

Example:

```bash
config firewall policy
    edit 1
        set srcintf port3
        set dstintf sdwan-1
        set action accept
        set srcaddr 172.16.205.0
        set dstaddr all
        set schedule always
        set service ALL
        set ssl-ssh-profile certificate-inspection
        set application-list g-default
    end
end
```

### Important

The firewall policy provides:

```text
Application Identification
+
Access Control
```

while the SD-WAN rule provides:

```text
Path Selection
```

So:

```text
Firewall Policy
      |
      +-- Allow / Deny
      +-- Application Detection
      |
      v
SD-WAN Rule
      |
      +-- SLA
      +-- Strategy
      +-- WAN Selection
```

